==============================================================================
4  --  RIGOROUS SINGLE-FIELD (one prime) REALIZATION BOUND
==============================================================================
  A pair of label sets collides mod p iff p divides the norm of a
  nonzero element of Z[zeta_F] whose coefficients lie in {-2..2}.
  |Norm| <= (2 P)^P, so each pair kills at most floor(P log2(2P)/
  log2 q_min) primes; the RowC envelope interval [2^250,
  2^250+2^128) holds ~ 2^128 / (phi(1024) ln 2^250) primes = 1 mod
  1024.  A family of size M is realizable in ONE such prime as
  soon as (M choose 2) * killed_per_pair < #primes.
  RowC 1/4    F=256 P=128  <=~4 primes killed/pair,  window holds ~2^111 primes  ->  rigorous M up to ~2^55   (8n^3 = 2^33)
  RowC 1/8    F=256 P=128  <=~4 primes killed/pair,  window holds ~2^111 primes  ->  rigorous M up to ~2^55   (8n^3 = 2^33)
  RowC 1/16   F=512 P=256  <=~10 primes killed/pair,  window holds ~2^111 primes  ->  rigorous M up to ~2^54   (8n^3 = 2^33)

